us":null,"result":"I'm rejecting PKT-0017. The executor's report says one of the goal's three requirements was not done: the goal asks for \"bug issues and fix commits per month or release\". Bug-issue counts are missing because `gh api` and WebFetch were refused. My instructions are to reject when the report says required work was not done, and the cause being outside the executor's control doesn't change that.\n\n**What is solid**\n- **Contract and scope:** the diff touches only `baseline.md`, a new script in `.theseus/oracle/perf/` and the packet file, with no source-code changes. That is 149 lines across 3 files, well within the budget.\n- **Packet records:** the executor log is filled in and nothing was spawned. Leaving it to humans to decide whether to port the missing upstream fixes is fine for an investigate packet, because the finding is in `baseline.md`.\n- **Numbers:** they match the tables. 231 of 871 fix commits is 26.5%, so \"27%\" holds, and 9 of 29 crash fixes is 31%.\n- **Limits stated:** the baseline says what the method can't show: the classification is by commit message, the jump in fix share comes from the `[bug]` tag convention, and \"timeout\" gives some false positives.\n\n**Weaknesses to fix when this is redone**\n1. **Crash rule doesn't match the docs.** In `defect-history.js`, `crash = fix && CRASH.test(...) || /\\bcrash/i.test(...)` also counts any commit mentioning \"crash\" as both crash-related and a fix, even without a fix keyword. Neither the script header nor `baseline.md` says so.\n2. **Script comment doesn't match the regex.** The comment says the fix pattern includes `issue`, but the `FIX` regex doesn't.\n3. **Deduplication can over-count.** Matching on (author date, subject) only removes rebased copies whose author date was kept. The jump to 402 commits in Euro-Office's 2025 against 291 in ONLYOFFICE's suggests some copies weren't removed, and the \"Euro-Office stopped tracking upstream around 2025-12\" claim depends on that. Both deserve a check.\n4. **One \"crash\" fix isn't a crash.** The \"upstream fixes not in Euro-Office\" list includes an SSRF fix (bug 82250). It is a real finding, but it should be labelled as a security fix.\n5. **Comparison not verified.** The comparison is by commit message only. Checking by content is left as a to-do in the baseline.\n\n**What must be done to pass**\n- Add bug-issue counts per month or per release from the Euro-Office/ONLYOFFICE issue trackers, which needs `gh api` or WebFetch allowed for the executor.\n- Or, if that access can't be granted, narrow the packet's goal to fix commits and spawn a separate packet for the bug-issue counts.\n- In both cases, fix the two documentation mismatches above.\n\nVERDICT: REJECT Goal requires bug-issue counts per month/release, which were not produced (gh/WebFetch refused); allow gh for the executor or narrow the goal and spawn an issues packet, and align the documented crash/fix rules with the script","ttft_ms":2483,"type":"result","duration_ms":19835,"uuid":"076ceddd-98a5-48ac-ac3d-200982fbdd91","ttft_stream_ms":1014,"time_to_request_ms":332,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":199,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":25,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":25,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":21,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":42,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":179,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":227,"process_anon_mib_result":139,"process_peak_rss_mib":255,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1010,"process_wall_ms_turn":19834,"process_cpu_ms_st